    "gangs": {
        "_doc": "Criminal organisations in the towns (src/systems/gangs.js). Each town, city and capital keeps settlement.underworld: its gangs (boss, crew, lieutenants, purse, stash of goods, turf, dens, rackets, wars) and its watch (a captain and a magistrate who can be bought, and the town's crackdown 0-100). Every coin is real: protection, dens, ransoms and black-market sales come out of the town's purse (Economy.drawTown); wages, recruits, bribes spent and openings go back into it; smuggled goods are bought from another realm's market stock and paid into that town's purse; fenced goods go into the town's market stock once cold. The week runs on its own seeded stream. Ranks: hanger-on -> soldier -> enforcer -> lieutenant -> boss.",
        "_tuning": "Tuned 2026-11 against the gangs' weekly drain on the towns' purses with GANGSIM=1 npx vitest run src/__tests__/gangs.econ.sim.test.js (the same worlds with and without gangs; the numbers are in docs/economy-balance.md). Protection, dens and the black market draw mostly on the town's purse, not its head count, and the townsfolk spend at most blackMarket.purseShare of it a week at the black market; lieutenantWage is an NPC lieutenant's wage (the player's own pay is their rank's weeklyPay).",
